text:
joni: heads-up: sample-app's Cloudflare Workers preview failed after we bumped @redwood/inference. error: ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND: fs when bundling.
liam: that's the classic node entry getting pulled in. did you import the package root?
joni: yep, just `import { createClient } from '@redwood/inference'` in the worker handler. wrangler build choked on require('fs') inside our internal node-utils.
sara: Workers don't have fs/Buffer/Node streams. We should have a worker/browser-safe ESM entry and an exports map so bundlers choose it automatically.
frank: quick repro: create a tiny worker that imports the package and does a ping; wrangler will show the same stack. The private node helpers are referenced unconditionally in the main bundle.
joni: short-term patch in the sample-app: point at our browser bundle directly `import { createClient } from '@redwood/inference/dist/index.browser.mjs'` and shim randomBytes with crypto.getRandomValues. works but it's ugly.
liam: also hit TS errors in the example app build: types mention NodeJS.ReadableStream and Buffer in a couple of exported interfaces. TS + DOM libs conflict in the worker env.
sara: proposed fixes: 1) split entrypoints: dist/index.browser.mjs (browser/edge), dist/index.node.cjs 2) exports map in package.json so bundlers pick the browser entry by default 3) move node-only helpers behind dynamic import so ESM packagers won't include them in browser bundles 4) produce separate node typings for node-only surface.
frank: sample snippet we can add to runtime to keep single-source but avoid bundling node parts:
```js
const isNode = typeof process !== 'undefined' && !!process.versions?.node;
export const getRandom = async (n) => {
  if (isNode) {
    const { randomBytes } = await import('crypto');
    return randomBytes(n);
  }
  const a = new Uint8Array(n);
  crypto.getRandomValues(a);
  return a;
};
```
joni: another subtle thing: our auth layer clones Request and passes it to a helper that streams to a Node ReadableStream. In edge flows we should keep the DOM Request/Response paths and avoid converting to Node streams at all.
liam: for types: we should stop exporting Node stream types from the shared APIs. Options: replace ReadableStream references with the universal WHATWG stream types or use conditional types on the node entry.
sara: I'll open an issue "edge-friendly ESM entry + typings audit" and list all the d.ts leaks. I'll grep for Buffer|fs|NodeJS|ReadableStream and paste results.
frank: I'll draft a small patch for v0.9.3: - add dist/index.browser.mjs and update package.json exports to prefer browser for ESM consumers - gate node helpers behind dynamic imports - fallback to crypto.getRandomValues when crypto.randomBytes isn't available - add a small worker smoke test in CI using wrangler preview.
joni: CI-bot: created issue #1482 and linked a sample-app PR with the quick hack.
liam: CI note: we should run a bundler+typecheck step with `lib: dom` enabled to catch worker-type regressions. frank, can you add that job?
frank: will do. also adding a lint rule to forbid direct `import fs` in client-facing modules.
sara: timeline: typings audit today, patch PR tomorrow, release patch ASAP. i'll coordinate with docs to add an "Edge runtime" note in the onboarding guide.
ci-bot: ci: worker-preview succeeded: https://preview.workers.example/xyz789
joni: thanks everyone. once the patch lands i'll remove our temporary shims in the sample app. :tada:
